law-paradox-dbae53d2.conceptual_definition:
This 'formula' expresses a profound conceptual relationship in fundamental physics concerning the origin of the arrow of time. It posits that the observed universal increase in entropy, described by the Second Law of Thermodynamics (
$\frac{dS}{dt} > 0$
), is fundamentally linked to a specific initial condition of the universe known as the Past Hypothesis. It suggests that the arrow of time is not an intrinsic property of microscopic laws (which are time-symmetric), but rather emerges from the universe beginning in a state of exceedingly low entropy.

relativistic-link-2ef9bd2d.conceptual_definition:
This formula is a generalized form of Ohm's Law that describes the current density (

 $ \mathbf{J} $

) in a conducting material that is moving with a velocity (

 $ \mathbf{v} $

) through a magnetic field (

 $ \mathbf{B} $

). It effectively combines the standard electrical conduction driven by an electric field (

 $ \mathbf{E} $

) with the electromotive force (EMF) induced by the conductor's motion through a magnetic field.

degenerate-core-heating-7828c932.conceptual_definition:
This equation is a fundamental thermodynamic relation that defines the infinitesimal change in heat (
\Delta Q
) transferred into or out of a system at a given absolute temperature (
\ T
) in terms of its change in entropy (
\Delta\delta\delta S
). In the context of "degenerate core heating," it describes the thermodynamic processes occurring within the dense, degenerate cores of stars, such as white dwarfs or the cores of massive stars prior to supernova, where heat exchange directly influences the entropy of the degenerate matter.

